// A union spelled with a BASE TYPE and a LITERAL of that base — `string | "err"` — in a
// function SIGNATURE. silent-class-inventory D1024, closed by the owner's 2026-09-02 ruling
// that a subsumed literal arm COLLAPSES: a union is a set of values, and an arm that adds no
// values adds no arm.
//
// Before the collapse the literal widened to a DUPLICATE `string` atom (the refusing sibling
// printed `…|string|…|string`), and because a union box's tags are POSITIONAL over the member
// set, the rep did not match what the function delivered: `vl check` rc 0 followed by
// `expected struct type at index 0, found (array (mut i32))`.
//
// THE CONTROL IS THE POINT OF THE PROBE AS MUCH AS THE COLLAPSE IS: `i32 | "err"` adds a
// value on both sides, so it must stay a genuine two-arm box and both of its arms must stay
// reachable. A probe that only showed the collapse would pass just as happily if the rule had
// eaten that union too.
//
// The other control — `Kind | "err"` staying a three-atom litunion — is in the FIXTURE
// (`tests/cases/literal-unions/subsumed-literal-arm-collapses.vl`) at its DECLARED spelling
// and NOT here, because the INLINE spelling of that union refuses for an unrelated
// pre-existing reason (`litunion-plus-literal-inline.vl`, measured identical on master).
// Carrying it here would have made this probe report D1024's own gap as still open.
//
// Should print err then ok then box-err.

function ret(n: i32): string | "err" {
  if n == 0 { return "err" }
  "ok"
}
function box(n: i32): i32 | "err" {
  if n == 0 { return "err" }
  5
}
print(ret(0))
print(ret(1))
const b = box(0)
if b is "err" { print("box-err") } else { print("box-num") }
